    <briefdescription>
<para>Standalone SHA-256 integrity verifier for ThemisDB modules. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Two usage patterns are supported:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Ad-hoc</bold> – call the static helpers to hash or compare a single file without constructing an instance.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Manifest-driven</bold> – load a JSON manifest that maps module names to their expected SHA-256 hashes and verify each module against it. The manifest format is a flat JSON object: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;themis_storage&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">:<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;e3b0c44298fc1c149…&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;themis_query&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">:<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a87ff679a2f3e71d9…&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread-safety: the static helpers are thread-safe. The manifest methods are NOT thread-safe; callers must synchronise external access if needed. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
